{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4917172","formula":"C₁₂H₁₉NS₂","hill":"C12H19NS2","elements":["H","C","N","S"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":19.0,"N":1.0,"S":2.0},"names":{"en":"Bis-TOM"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bis-TOM, or 2,5-TOM, also known as 4-methyl-2,5-dimethylthioamphetamine or as 2,5-dithio-DOM, is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine and amphetamine families related to DOM. It is the analogue of DOM in which the methoxy groups at the 2 and 5 positions have been replaced with methylthio groups. In his book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved) and other publications, Alexander Shulgin lists bis-TOM's dose as greater than 160 mg orally and its duration as unknown. The effects of bis-TOM have been reported to include vague awareness of something and \"a suggestion of darting, physically (when going to sleep)\", but no mental effects."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":15915353,"mass":241.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=C(C=C1SC)CC(C)N)SC","inchikey":"XFCQINWERPNOHI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[4-methyl-2,5-bis(methylsulfanyl)phenyl]propan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"15915353","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.739,"y":2.42,"z":-0.367,"el":"S"},{"x":-3.273,"y":-1.504,"z":-0.297,"el":"S"},{"x":4.023,"y":-1.242,"z":-0.032,"el":"N"},{"x":1.824,"y":-0.659,"z":-0.955,"el":"C"},{"x":2.593,"y":-1.161,"z":0.28,"el":"C"},{"x":0.481,"y":-0.053,"z":-0.626,"el":"C"},{"x":0.345,"y":1.3,"z":-0.352,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.618,"y":-0.901,"z":-0.608,"el":"C"},{"x":2.123,"y":-2.541,"z":0.742,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.028,"y":0.975,"z":-0.033,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.878,"y":-0.385,"z":-0.31,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.916,"y":1.817,"z":-0.054,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.358,"y":1.575,"z":0.291,"el":"C"},{"x":1.722,"y":3.043,"z":1.336,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.778,"y":-2.686,"z":0.987,"el":"C"},{"x